"""Per-peptide Quick answers, dosing sections and FAQs. Every number comes from an FDA label (DailyMed) or a cited abstract."""
DM=lambda s:f"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid={s}"
OZ,RYB,WEG,MOU,ZEP="42bdd912-2393-44c4-b7e0-47672ca28991","27f15fac-7d98-4114-a2ec-92494a91da98","ee06186f-2aa3-4990-a760-757579d8f77b","c1ceb7ca-9976-4ac1-b45c-3975de8aac4c","487cd7e7-434c-4925-99fa-aa80b1cc776b"
def L(s,t): return f'<a href="{DM(s)}" rel="noopener">{t}</a>'
def pm(i,t): return f'<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/{i}/" rel="noopener">{t}</a>'
PRESC='<p class="note"><strong>Your prescriber sets your dose.</strong> This is a summary of the official FDA label to help you follow along, not a plan to start, change, or stop anything.</p>'
RQ=["What is actually in the product, and has it been third-party tested?","Is there any human evidence for my specific goal, or only animal studies?","Could it interact with my other medicines or conditions?","Is there an FDA-approved option for what I'm trying to treat?","How would we know if it's working, or causing harm?"]
RQHTML="<h3>Good questions to bring to a clinician</h3><ul>"+"".join(f"<li>{q}</li>" for q in RQ)+"</ul>"
WHYCONF='<h3>Why the numbers online don\'t agree</h3><ul><li>Many online "protocols" are converted from animal studies, where doses are set by body weight in rats or mice. Those don\'t translate directly to people.</li><li>The few human reports use different routes and settings, with no agreed standard.</li><li>Unregulated products can vary in what they actually contain.</li><li>Sellers and influencers often share numbers without sources.</li></ul><p>See <a href="../why-peptide-info-is-confusing.html">Why is peptide info so confusing?</a></p>'
